{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/826379-how-do-you-use-hunters-when-you-re-playing-the-other-games","id":826379,"title":"How Do You Use Hunters When You're Playing The Other Games?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-08T16:32:48-08:00","id":826379,"title":"How Do You Use Hunters When You're Playing The Other Games?","content":"How pervasive is the fear of the sheep becoming wolves? What methods do they use to hunt you down? How do you fight back? How stable are the occasional alliances? <br /> <br /> I, for one, feel like a game with supernatural PCs and not a single confrontation with a Hunter is very strange. If they never strike or cause any trouble, why all the skulking and sneaking around?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T16:43:55-08:00","id":826384,"title":"","content":"I find a lot of supernatural games I hear about from others tend to have a lot of focus on those supernaturals. If you aren't going out of your way to do things in public and attract attention, and the worst acts are between fellow monsters, a hunter's suspicion is not likely to be raised.<br /> <br /> In my own games, generally humanity is pretty much like it is in real life. Not everyone is a hero waiting for the monster to appear, and when the monster appears they won't act like they did in all their fantasies and will probably excuse themselves over it later. Better to be safe than risk the horrors of that other world. But some people do end up becoming hunters and they tend to be either horribly misguided or focused. Even at that point it's rare to find one who's actually good at it.<br /> <br /> To be completely fair to the players of other game lines, the hunters usually have to be at least a <i>little</i> bad at it. It's not exactly fair if halfway through your first session you're told that your character was staked and beheaded by a vampire hunter they never knew existed and never had a chance to know.<br /> <br /> So whether they're misguided or focused, they tend to be sloppy or flamboyant. Both cases offer a chance for the players to notice and react. Either the hunters bumble through or they announce themselves broadly, enough to put the PCs on guard. Occasionally I've tied hunters into the pasts of characters, allowing them a reprieve from their depredations based on 'old times,' but one that shouldn't be tested.<br /> <br /> In our last game the players encountered a hunter in his lair, not knowing he was a hunter, and while he was unprepared still managed to drive them off with his martial skill. The whole thing was hilarious, and made the characters very angry, because he was arrogant and boastful about it as he was pummeling them and they didn't manage to lay a finger on him before running away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T16:56:32-08:00","id":826392,"title":"","content":"Humorously, I feel the opposite: if you're in a supernatural game and you have a Cell on your trail, you've been careless and you screwed up. And even then, realistically you would have to mess up a lot: every incident doesn't call down a Hunter cell.<br /> <br /> As an ST, Hunters are occasionally a sort of speed bump if they do come up, but mostly are just a &quot;hey you guys have messed up&quot;...but usually that's the role of other supernaturals. Vampires police Vampires, Werewolves content with spirits, other werewolves, and any sort of spirit wizard, so on and so forth.<br /> <br /> <br /> And, as always, the sad truth is that if a group of supernatural characters can't deal with hunters, they assuredly can't deal with their actual antagonists. There's a reason that the Hunter bokks gives you weakened versions of the other splats to fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T16:56:44-08:00","id":826393,"title":"","content":"I didn't say that Hunters in other games needed to operate quickly, often and hyper-competently. In fact, these sloppy and flamboyant Hunters are appropriate to the beginnings of a Chronicle. The veteran Hunters with the mightiest Endowments should come up later. Escalation of difficulty, and all that.<br /> <br /> Did the invading Hunter ask the characters to show him their moves?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T17:02:39-08:00","id":826400,"title":"","content":"Hunters make great deniable assets. <br /> <br /> I don't think the average supernatural society has much to fear from the average human (save for maybe Prometheans), if only because mortals know so little about them. That changes when you have the local cell/compact/conspiracy receive some interesting intelligence form a shadowy patron that just so happens to know what weapons work best on werewolves, or where the local vampires sleep, or where the mummy has his artifacts stashed. When the cold war between factions goes hot, most if the action is done by mortal pawns who have no fucking clue what they're mixed up in; damn near every line has some sort of faction representing leadership of a Cult.<br /> <br /> Vampires rat each other out to hunters often, allowing one to damage their enemy without the loss of face associated with a more explicit attack; like we see in Berlin, hunters can even become a bona fide part of the Kindred establishment. Werewolf packs can easily get into what look for all the world like mundane gang turf wars. The Guardians, Ladder, and Seers all have tons of dedicated mortals in their pockets, and every Mastigos out there has the ability to implant a Manchruian Candidate assassination mission into anyone on the street. Fights between Arisen can span continents and centuries; I'm sure portions of the Crusades and Inquisition had Iremite hands moving the pieces. <br /> <br /> Of course, the fun in all this is when things spiral out of control. Having your own private hit squad is great right up until they start picking their own targets and your child or packmate or mentor winds up on the wrong side of a suicide bombing. I'm sure more than a few Seers have been caught in Division Six's sights, just as surely as VALKYRIE has iced a few wrong vampires or Arisen cults have self-destructed (like the Faithful of Shulpae may have).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T19:00:12-08:00","id":826464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/826379-how-do-you-use-hunters-when-you-re-playing-the-other-games?p=826393#post826393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say that Hunters in other games needed to operate quickly, often and hyper-competently. In fact, these sloppy and flamboyant Hunters are appropriate to the beginnings of a Chronicle. The veteran Hunters with the mightiest Endowments should come up later. Escalation of difficulty, and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's typically immersion-breaking for me if a sloppy, incompetent Hunter is somehow also a good enough investigator to find my players. Though, again, I tend to have players that are cautious enough to not get on radars in the first place. Though I DO have one or two that have some &quot;subtlety&quot; problems. . .they've had more problems with police than Hunters, though.<br /> <br /> Lest I come off as too negative, Hunter is by far my favorite game to run. I find it's themes and atmosphere to be astounding. They just can't hang with the big boys unless some weird shit is happening (like. . a neonate against a senior member of the Lucifuge).<br /> <br /> In my current game, which features a Dark Hero from Mirrors, a Fetch, and a Lucifuge who found a fun little grimoire and got Witch Finder's Gutter Magic, the Lucifuge is getting tracked down by Cheiron after (basically) letting himself get tricked into working for them for a bit. However, he found a nearby Cell's &quot;17 year old witches are perfectly good Potential Assets&quot; strategy a little unacceptable, But now he's framed for setting her on fire, killing one of the Cheiron and shooting the other (who, of course, were simply Concerned Citizens), got very brief national attention, and the rest of the Cell is gunning after him pretty hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T05:08:09-08:00","id":826709,"title":"","content":"I like to run it one of two ways. One way has a group of hunters as antagonists in a story line, or side antagonists and a sub-plot. Maybe there is a plot-driven reason to have a group of Hunters in the game. It shouldn't feel forced though, it should flow with the plot.<br /> <br /> The other way I like to run it is to have the &quot;dice of doom&quot;. This is for when a character screws up and does something that can't not be noticed, public denial of the supernatural be damned. I roll a d3 to determine the tier of hunters coming after him, a d10 to determine the number of hunters on his tail, and in the case of tiers 2 and 3 I roll a d10 to determine the group coming after him, with each number corresponding to a different Compact or Conspiracy depending on the tier. That's more forced and artificial, but it's also reminiscent of the &quot;random encounter&quot; dice of certain other table top games I could mention...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10065,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10065-zolace","user":"Zolace","date":".  I typed d20 for the roll to determine the hunter group, I meant d10. 02-09-2016, 09:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10065-zolace","name":"Zolace","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T08:38:16-08:00","id":826846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/826379-how-do-you-use-hunters-when-you-re-playing-the-other-games?p=826400#post826400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, the fun in all this is when things spiral out of control. Having your own private hit squad is great right up until they start picking their own targets and your child or packmate or mentor winds up on the wrong side of a suicide bombing. I'm sure more than a few Seers have been caught in Division Six's sights, just as surely as VALKYRIE has iced a few wrong vampires or Arisen cults have self-destructed (like the Faithful of Shulpae may have).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, this. It was the best of times when two conspiracies of supernaturals both thought they controlled the same Hunter group in their war against each other, only for it to be co-opted from within in the confusion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T22:38:15-08:00","id":827329,"title":"","content":"I've used Hunters twice now. The first was in Vampire, the hunters took out some of the locals and the Sheriff gave the players the task of doing clean up. It gave them the chance to face humans who actually knew how to fight back, not the cake walk they expected.<br /> \u200bThe second time is in my current Mage chronicle, though here the hunters are purely background. I've adopted the Strix as opponents and the players have found reason to research a group of hunters descended from Rome that specialize in hunting the birds of Dis. A cell of the hunters are at work in the city but the goal is just to provide an avenue for the mages to use their information gathering skills to learn some of the Strix weaknesses and history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T13:39:52-08:00","id":829860,"title":"","content":"This'll be my first game, but I have a couple of Lucifuge who will serve as regular NPCs in a game of Geist I'll be hosting, be it as supporting or inhibiting forces. I chose them because, well, as far as Hunters go Lucifuge tend to be a bit more understanding of the monsters, and &quot;Mortal Remains&quot; describes them as taking Sin Eaters as a case-by-case basis. I feel that while Hunters by and large aren't that competent when thrown into the ring with all the other supernaturals out there, nor that trustworthy, there are exceptions to every rule. Plus, occasionally having actual demons to fight instead of ghosts, abmortals or Ghost Trees to fight would spice things up a bit, and given one Hunter can understand all (mortal) spoken language and the other can throw hellfire about, they can prove useful as allies, albeit ones who'll want some info in return to understand Sin Eater culture.<br /> <br /> I may be going about this wrong, really. *shrugs*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T16:33:49-08:00","id":829906,"title":"","content":"My general guideline is that any hunter cells able to survive more than say, a month, is tough enough, smart enough and clever enough to become a threat, especially if they're part of an organization that can provide backing and training (MM, TF:V, etc)<br /> <br /> Those who aren't generally go in two directions:<br /> <br /> 1. Messy death. Self-explanatory.<br /> 2. Pawns, like atamajakki said. Case in point:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/826379-how-do-you-use-hunters-when-you-re-playing-the-other-games?p=826464#post826464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's typically immersion-breaking for me if a sloppy, incompetent Hunter is somehow also a good enough investigator to find my players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, those guys don't do their own investigations. They get mysterious phone calls and evidence in the mail (no return address) from people who <i>are</i> competent. If a sloppy, incompetent Hunter cell shows up at your door-step it means you have a bigger problem on your hands.<br /> <br /> Also note that nothing prevents a Hunter from being the one pulling the strings on another, less experienced Hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 02-27-2016, 12:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T03:38:30-08:00","id":830127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/826379-how-do-you-use-hunters-when-you-re-playing-the-other-games?p=829906#post829906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, those guys don't do their own investigations. They get mysterious phone calls and evidence in the mail (no return address) from people who <i>are</i> competent. If a sloppy, incompetent Hunter cell shows up at your door-step it means you have a bigger problem on your hands.<br /> <br /> Also note that prevents a Hunter from being the one pulling the string on another, less experienced Hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's. . .better, but is also a whole other can of worms. I often wonder (this is non-accusatory) how often other STs go through the steps of &quot;how do the antagonists know about X&quot;. If the Hunters now know where the players live, how? Like, specifically, not just &quot;someone smarter told them&quot;, but how did THAT person know. If they're being surveilled, do they give their players the appropriate rolls (even if the ST does the rolls themselves) to notice the dude with the camera, or the cars tailing them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T06:49:31-08:00","id":830207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/826379-how-do-you-use-hunters-when-you-re-playing-the-other-games?p=830127#post830127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's. . .better, but is also a whole other can of worms. I often wonder (this is non-accusatory) how often other STs go through the steps of &quot;how do the antagonists know about X&quot;. If the Hunters now know where the players live, how? Like, specifically, not just &quot;someone smarter told them&quot;, but how did THAT person know. If they're being surveilled, do they give their players the appropriate rolls (even if the ST does the rolls themselves) to notice the dude with the camera, or the cars tailing them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, now that's is a can of worms I can answer!<br /> <br /> Read &quot;How to Hide From the Internet&quot; by Mike Bazzell and &quot;How to be Invisible, 3rd edition&quot; By J. J. Luna. They go into detail about how to be anonymous in the modern age. People give out alarming amounts of personal data without realizing it or even thinking twice about it. Bruce Schiener goes into detail in &quot;Data and Goliath.&quot; That's hefty reading list to be sure, but if you're interested in this topic, it's a place to start.<br /> <br /> Any group that relies on information for survival, be it for legitimate purposes like a newspaper or for less than legit purposes like organized crime or a community of monsters, (who operate almost exactly like organized crime) becomes very, very good at having feelers out: sympathetic ears in the local police department, contacts in relevant industries, established sources, etc.<br /> <br /> For supernatural groups, the ability to recruit sources and gather information is magnified a hundred fold. Vampire have networks of ghouls: ultra loyal agents kept in line with blood addiction, some of which have been in place for centuries, to supplement Auspex. Werewolves have a terrifying array of senses, spirits to watch their back and vast support networks. Demons can give a person <i>whatever they want</i> in exchange for information or obedience.<br /> <br /> Now, imagine you've just confronted the supernatural for the first time, what's the first thing you do? Buy a gun? Start researching the occult? Do your players know how to do these things without tipping off the authorities or using the internet?<br /> <br /> As for what kind of rolls players need to avoid detection, I recommend a narrative-based approach to drive home that they are no longer safe in their ignorance, and need to be careful every single day.<br /> <br /> Make your players buy merits like Anonymity and Safe Place, and emphasize that these represent <i>major</i> life-style changes to avoid detection: cash purchases at the grocery store, online purchases are made using temporary credit cards under an assumed name, houses and cars are owned through a New Mexico holding corporation (seriously), internet use requires sandboxing, a VPN, and Tor. As for rolls, I recommend Wits + Investigation+Contacts to get advance warning of someone looking for them, and Manipulation + Subterfuge to control the information they give. Have them make resource spends to get the necessary computer equipment and invest XP in specialties like &quot;cover online tracks.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hiding from the opposition shouldn't be a roll or fail thing, it should be an <i>atmosphere</i> thing: this is what the World of Darkness is like, and this is how separated from average humanity a Hunter has to be to operate safely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 07-23-2016, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T08:34:10-08:00","id":830250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/826379-how-do-you-use-hunters-when-you-re-playing-the-other-games?p=830127#post830127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's. . .better, but is also a whole other can of worms. I often wonder (this is non-accusatory) how often other STs go through the steps of &quot;how do the antagonists know about X&quot;. If the Hunters now know where the players live, how? Like, specifically, not just &quot;someone smarter told them&quot;, but how did THAT person know. If they're being surveilled, do they give their players the appropriate rolls (even if the ST does the rolls themselves) to notice the dude with the camera, or the cars tailing them?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I suppose it depends on the game/context. In Vampire, for instance, some other rival Kindred might know or suspect this info and distribute it. For Werewolf, the Pack's general territory is likely known. Mages love finding out info about things (which likely extends to each other). Etc.<br /> <br /> Another thing to keep in mind. Provided your mystery antagonist knows some Hunter Cells they can sic on targets, it's relatively low cost just to point them at targets they merely <i>suspect</i>. IE, the foe doesn't need to know your Haven's location (for instance), if they have an idea of where you loiter. They can just point the Cell at a target and wait for confirmation (or nothing).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T13:03:36-08:00","id":830438,"title":"","content":"Don't forget to be fair when NPCs attempt to track down your PCs. Consider what the players have done to protect themselves and then decide if it's not only possible for the antagonist to overcome those defenses but if it's reasonable that he would have taken those steps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T08:17:30-08:00","id":831748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/826379-how-do-you-use-hunters-when-you-re-playing-the-other-games?p=830207#post830207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, now thats is a can of worms I can answer!<br /> <br /> Read &amp;quot;How to Hide From the Internet&amp;quot; by Mike Bazzell and &amp;quot;How to be Invisible, 3rd edition&amp;quot; By J. J. Luna. Those two authors go into great detail about what a person needs to do be anonymous in the modern age. You give out an incredible amount of data without even realizing it. Bruce Schiener goes into detail in &amp;quot;Data and Goliath.&amp;quot; A hefty reading list to be sure, but if you're really interested in this topic, that's the place to start.<br /> <br /> When you're a group that relies on information for survival, be it for legitimate purposes like a news paper or for less than legit purposes like organized crime or a community of monsters, (who operate almost exactly like organized crime) very, very good at have feelers out: sympathetic ears in the local police department, contacts in relevant industries, and established sources.<br /> <br /> For supernatural groups, this ability to recruit sources and gather information is magnified a hundred fold. Vampires, in addition to Auspex have the ability to create ghouls: ultra loyal agents keep in line with blood addiction and the entrenchment that comes from having these networks in places for centuries. Werewolves have a terrifying array of senses, as well as the ability to recruit spirits to watch their back and vast support networks. Demons can give a person <i>whatever they want</i> in exchange for information or obedience.<br /> <br /> Now, imagine you've just been confronted with the supernatural, what's the first thing you do? Buy a gun? Start researching the occult? Do your players know how to do these things without tipping off the authorities or using the internet?<br /> <br /> As for what kind of rolls players need to avoid detection, I recommend a more narrative-based approach to drive home that they are no longer safe in their ignorance, and need to be careful every single day.<br /> <br /> Make your players buy merits like Anonymity and Safe Place, and emphasize that these represent <i>major</i> life-style changes to avoid detection: cash purchases at the grocery store, online purchases are made using temporary credit cards under an assumed name, houses and cars are owned through a New Mexico holding corporation (seriously), internet use requires sandboxing, a VPN, and Tor. As for rolls, I recommend Wits + Investigation+Contacts to get advance warning of someone looking for them, and Manipulation + Subterfuge to control the information they give. Have them make resource spends to get the necessary computer equipment and invest XP in specialties like &amp;quot;cover online tracks.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Hiding from the opposition shouldn't be a roll or fail thing, it should be an <i>atmosphere</i> thing: this is what the World of Darkness is like, and this is how separated from average humanity a Hunter has to be to operate safely.</div> </div> </div> </div>What a fantastic response! I'll have to check those books out; as an IT guy and a friend of a former skip-tracer, it's a subject I have an interest in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T19:33:06-08:00","id":832264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/826379-how-do-you-use-hunters-when-you-re-playing-the-other-games?p=831748#post831748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What a fantastic response! I'll have to check those books out; as an IT guy and a friend of a former skip-tracer, it's a subject I have an interest in.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries.<br /> <br /> Now to give you the other side of the situation, why even newbie hunters aren't <i>completely</i> screwed. Hunters have tactical and strategic advantages they can leverage, <i>if</i> they're alert and clever. Most of this is privileged information since hunters can't just buy splat books on drivethrurpg, but intelligence-gathering and investigation are part of the job. I recommend Counterinsurgency by David Kilcullen for insight here.<br /> <br /> <b>Monsters are not Monoliths:</b> both in terms of agendas and in terms of resources. For a new Hunter, it's easy to imagine a vast monster conspiracy that controls all aspects of media and government. In truth, monsters are a patchwork of insular tribes and micro-states. Monsters have extensive resources, but those resources are already committed to counteracting other threats. A vampire Prince isn't just watching out for hunter cells. She needs to guard against other Princes cutting in on her territory, the Strix, ambitious rivals and other dangers. Going full thermonuclear war on a hunter cell is an overreaction that signals weakness. Hell, if the hunter cell knocks out a rival, she may send them candy and flowers.<br /> <br /> <b>Monsters have geographic limits on their power:</b> If a cell based in Chicago fights a vampire dwelling in Houston, the offended vampire has a few options, none of them good: make the very dangerous trek across multiple states to enact revenge, then ask for permission to operate in a distant city from that city's prince, or ask the prince to deliver revenge of his behalf (in exchange for another favor, and the Prince will assign a Neonate whose heart isn't in the job). A werewolf who tastes your blood can track you across dimensions, true, but to get to you he might have to cross the territory of multiple hostile packs, and abandon his own territory. A changeling will be loath to abandon the protection of her Court's Bulwark.<br /> <br /> <b>Monsters are not irrational or unwilling to negotiate:</b> There was a spirited discussion on this board about hunter-monster friendships and alliances. The default setting is that this happens <i>very</i> rarely, and there is substantial prejudice against it, with monster-sympathetic cells being called &quot;cancer cells&quot; by hard-liners. That said, multiple conspiracies and compacts are informed enough to know when non-violent interaction is a reasonable possibility. In real life, hostile forces <i>do</i> negotiate with each other. During the recent occupation of Iraq the most successful commanders were the ones able to start and maintain a dialogue with insurgent forces. Many monsters have castes dedicated to negotiation and conflict resolution, what form this negotiation takes can vary, anything from an idealistic Uratha Edoloth (&quot;hey, we have mutual goals and enemies, let's have coffee,&quot;) to a Spring Court Emissary bearing lore of the True Fae (&quot;this is what we have to deal with, and if we go away it's what <i>you</i> have to deal with&quot;), or a vampire neonate offering a combination of rewards and threats (&quot;Nice family, shame if anything happened to them&quot;), but your players can interact with Monsters in ways that don't automatically involve violence.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, 2nd edition enforces the psychological toll of violence, even for monsters. Killing humans is a breaking point for just about every splat. A trigger-happy Vampire, Werewolf, Changeling, etc. is going to ding their humanity stat and eventually become a liability to themselves and their society.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, monsters with a Masquerade to maintain realize that unnecessary violence is a complicated mess to clean up.<br /> <br /> <b>Organizational support and training</b>: Is one of your hunters a VASCU agent, a member of MM, TFV or any other organization that has resources and an institutional memory? Then they have an operational security &quot;best practices&quot; document for new members. Even if a Hunter cell is completely cut off, there are institutions that can reach out to them, notably the VASCU field liaison office. A hunter cell may meet the liaison officer in an interrogation room... or the liaison might do the smart thing and reach out to a cell before they get themselves in trouble, and hand them the Unofficial World of Darkness Hunter's Survival Guide.<br /> <br /> <b>Social networks:</b> Even ones the cell is not aware of. A hunter who saves a family from rampaging werewolves now has someone willing to provide an alibi and a place to stay. If the Vampires have an agent-in-place at a local police station, other cops might make small efforts to stymie the mole's efforts to track hunters. Since crooked cops tend to rely on the police version of <i>omerta</i> rather than good operational security, word will get around that desk sergeant Willie McGhoul is &quot;has a part-time job, after work, during work, nudge-nudge, wink-wink.&quot;<br /> The cell might receive an anonymous call that goes &quot;Two cops are going to show up at your door in fifteen minutes, they don't have warrant, they're not on official police business. Politely but firmly refuse to let them in. If they ask where you were last night, you were at Bernie's Bowling Alley. Bernie knows the drill and will vouch for you.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 06-11-2016, 01:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T10:05:18-08:00","id":839274,"title":"","content":"In our game, it became a running joke of &quot;So a Vampire walks in to a Hunter bar...&quot;. Which actually happened during game play when one PC told another PC, who had recently been turned into a vampire, to meet him at a particular roadhouse type bar at the city outskirts. It just so happened that this bar was a Hunter hangout a la Supernatural. Hijinks ensued, and much fun making was had.<br /> <br /> We run a crossover &quot;friendly&quot; game. The various splats have territories in whatever city we are playing in at the time. It contributes to the monster of the week scenarios that I like to sprinkle around to make the overall metaplot relevant long term.<br /> <br /> When running a Hunter centric game, the other splats are hazards and targets of opportunity. It is also possible that in their often short careers, a Hunter may become infected, turned, controlled, or otherwise become the monster he/she once hated.<br /> <br /> In a game that is centered around the other splats, Hunter involvement becomes a boogyman, a threat to hang over their heads. They are used as examples of what comes when you break the masquerade or other thematic restraint on staying hidden.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10978-azenogoth","name":"Azenogoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10978_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T13:23:58-08:00","id":840144,"title":"","content":"Genius+Changeling+Hunter=Best Bros.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}